<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <RootNamespace>Holdfast</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Holdfast</AssemblyName>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Metadatos del paquete -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>Holdfast</PackageId>
    <Version>0.2.0</Version>
    <Authors>Diego Gerardo Larrosa</Authors>
	<Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 Diego Gerardo Larrosa</Copyright>
    <Description>
      Arena allocator with typed handles and intrusive collections for .NET.
      Fixed-size blocks, no per-node GC objects, stable handles for the lifetime
      of the node. Includes a doubly linked list and two red-black trees.
      Built for long-running, single-threaded workloads with very large working
      sets: 24 bytes per key and roughly half the insert time of SortedSet at
      50 million keys.
    </Description>
    <PackageTags>arena;allocator;handle;slotmap;red-black-tree;memory;collections;gc-free;low-allocation;serialization;checkpoint</PackageTags>

    <!-- Lo que mira quien ya tiene la version anterior instalada y le aparece
         que hay una nueva. Vacio en la 0.1.0, que para una primera version
         esta bien; a partir de la segunda no. -->
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
Checkpoints. The 0.1.0 README claimed the arena was position-independent and that
checkpointing cost a file write, without an API to do it. Now there is one.

- Snapshot writes a set of arenas and named roots to a stream and reads them back.
  The file is the blocks verbatim: no traversal, no pointer fixup. A Handle written
  down before the save is the same value after the load, and points at the same node.
- AddSet, AddList, AddTree and AddHandle pull in the arenas they need. AddTree adds
  two of them, because a RedBlackTree keeps its nodes in Arena&lt;ArenaList&lt;T&gt;&gt;
  and its values in Arena&lt;T&gt;.
- ArenaState&lt;T&gt; is an arena's state as an object; Arena&lt;T&gt;.Capture, Restore
  and Swap move it around. The storage stays static, so the hot path is unchanged.
- Where it loses: the file weighs the reserved capacity rather than the live keys;
  every checkpoint is the whole arena, with no incremental writes and no compression;
  T must hold no references; and a file only loads on the same byte order and the
  same node layout. All of it is in the README.

68 tests, up from 42. No breaking changes.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/diegolarrosa/Holdfast</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/diegolarrosa/Holdfast</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>

    <!-- SourceLink viene incluido en el SDK de .NET 8: con estas dos
         propiedades el que depure puede entrar al codigo fuente. -->
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="../../README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
	  
	<!-- La expresion SPDX enlaza al texto generico de MIT, que no lleva TU
         aviso de copyright. Y MIT exige preservar ese aviso en toda copia.
         Asi que los dos archivos viajan dentro del paquete. -->
	<None Include="../../LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
	<None Include="../../THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Las pruebas y el banco tocan miembros internal (Arena.N, Handle.Raw,
       constructores). Sin esto no compilan como proyectos separados. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Holdfast.Tests" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Holdfast.Benchmarks" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
